{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:OrganicChemistry.ThreadingLink","@type":"LeanModule","name":"OrganicChemistry.ThreadingLink","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.GCD.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Parity","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Group.Nat"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.half_efficiency","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.half_efficiency","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/threading-link.lean#L63-L72","doc":"The threading efficiency: alexander weight / pairwise weight = 1/2\nfor even N. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.alexanderWeightAtOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.alexanderWeightAtOne","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/threading-link.lean#L55-L61","doc":"Alexander weight of T(2,2m) at q=1 is m = N/2.\nThis is half the pairwise weight N.\n(Only valid for even N.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.numCrossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.numCrossings","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/threading-link.lean#L50-L53","doc":"Number of crossings in the standard braid representation\n(σ₁σ₂⋯σ_{N-1})²: always 2(N-1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.one_component_of_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.one_component_of_odd","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/threading-link.lean#L43-L48","doc":"T(2,N) is a knot (1 component) when N is odd. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.two_components_of_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.two_components_of_even","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/threading-link.lean#L36-L41","doc":"T(2,N) is a 2-component link when N is even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.numComponents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.numComponents","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/threading-link.lean#L32-L34","doc":"Number of components of T(2,N) = gcd(2,N). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.atoms_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.atoms_ge","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/threading-link.lean#L30-L30","doc":"At least 3 atoms for a ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.atoms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.atoms","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/threading-link.lean#L28-L28","doc":"Number of atoms threaded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink.mk","kind":"ctor","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/threading-link.lean#L26-L26","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.ThreadingLink","kind":"structure","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/threading-link.lean#L22-L30","doc":"The threading link T(2,N) for a ring of N atoms.\nFor even N, this is a 2-component torus link.\nFor odd N, it is a torus knot. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:threading-link","label":"def:threading-link","md":"quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/threading-link.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}